## 7. Conversation Snapshot: Prevalidation Before Restore

**Component:** `include/strata/core/conversation_snapshot.hpp` — `conversation_snapshot_validate()`

**Responsibilities:** Validates every layer and checkpoint of a `SavedConversation` against the current session geometry before any CUDA call or destination write.

**Change:** The declaration exists but the header does not expose a way to validate only the geometry array (the 18-element `geometry` field of `SavedConversation`). Add a lightweight geometry-only check so the serve loop can reject a snapshot from a different model without touching K/V buffers.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/conversation_snapshot.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/conversation_snapshot.hpp
@@ -55,6 +55,14 @@ bool conversation_snapshot_validate(const SavedConversation& image, const Sessio
                                     const ModelGeometry& g, const QsaState& draft, std::string& error);

+/// Geometry-only check: the 18-element runtime compatibility array and the layer carve.
+/// No K/V or checkpoint validation; safe to call before any device allocation.
+inline bool conversation_geometry_validate(const SavedConversation& image, const ModelGeometry& g,
+                                           int64_t layer_lo, int64_t layer_hi, std::string& error) {
+    if (image.layer_lo != layer_lo || image.layer_hi != layer_hi) {
+        error = "snapshot layer carve [" + std::to_string(image.layer_lo) + "," + std::to_string(image.layer_hi) +
+                "] does not match the session's [" + std::to_string(layer_lo) + "," + std::to_string(layer_hi) + "]";
+        return false;
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
 enum class ConversationRestore { restored, invalid, transfer_failed };
```

**Verification cases:**
1. A snapshot captured on a single-GPU session (layer_lo=0, layer_hi=48) restored into a split stage (layer_lo=18, layer_hi=48) → returns false with the mismatch message.
2. Matching carve → returns true.

